  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "All-atom generative frameworks, cross-state allosteric prediction and physics-grounded energetics are pushing structure modeling past static single-pose outputs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is treating a protein or complex as a distribution of states with associated energetics, not a single predicted pose. OriDynamics targets all-atom ensemble generation for monomers and complexes with ligands or partners; Cadense produces antibody Fv ensembles from sequence trained against MD-derived distributions; transition-corridor dynamical fingerprints rank microscopic participants in rare A-B transitions; AllositeUltra predicts allosteric sites on both apo and substrate-bound structures using a cross-state benchmark. A second strand injects physics into learned representations: HEIWA adds explicit-implicit solvent attention to ESM3 embeddings, AIMNet2-CPCM computes solvated ligand strain across thousands of PDB ligands, and an antisymmetrized evolutionary ddG predictor is averaged with JanusDDG to enforce thermodynamic consistency. Docking work is more sceptical: focused torsional supervision gave no gain over broad score-field continuation in DiffDock post-training, and Pyrite frames cofolded pose selection as an agentic ranking benchmark.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
